#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186353666 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6329ab32-968f-5041-b2e3-12dde408968a" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Function on Which to Apply a Root-Finding Method When Applying the Implicit Euler Method"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "90fb1a44-20f8-535d-b1ee-9b00d537ac30" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "g({y}_{\\text{new}})=-\\,y-0.5({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353668} {:answer/id #uuid "a42303f7-0d09-5502-b0ae-9ced5f9cc56d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "g({y}_{\\text{new}})=-{y}_{\\text{new}}+y-0.5({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353669} {:answer/id #uuid "3cd44607-79c3-5421-916f-a4d02e3d47fd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "g({y}_{\\text{new}})={y}_{\\text{new}}-y-0.5({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353670} {:answer/id #uuid "b83c8bcb-15ac-59ae-92e3-33db5021e93a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "g({y}_{\\text{new}})={y}_{\\text{new}}-y-{y}_{\\text{new}}-0.5({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353671} {:answer/id #uuid "b86a3758-3dd5-53da-b15e-0089d9bcc1e9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "g({y}_{\\text{new}})=-\\,y-0.5{y}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353672}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "90fb1a44-20f8-535d-b1ee-9b00d537ac30" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "g({y}_{\\text{new}})=-\\,y-0.5({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353668} :answer-field/id #uuid "a60dc863-e46e-5888-a139-a1ce74c38570" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353667}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3e1fd1e0-f9ee-5efd-85cc-903531185842" :question/math-academy-id "q-333105" :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}={x}^{2}+2y,\\,y(0)=0\n$$\n\nUsing the implicit Euler method with step size $Δx=0.5,$ the new value ${y}_{\\text{new}}$ is obtained by solving the equation $g({y}_{\\text{new}})=0$ at each step.\nWhich of the following is the **general form** of $g({y}_{\\text{new}})$ in terms of the new values ${x}_{\\text{new}}$ and ${y}_{\\text{new}},$ and the current value $y?$" :question/worked-solution "For an initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=f(x,y),\\,{y}_{0}=y({x}_{0}),\n$$\n\nthe implicit Euler method with step size $Δx$ is given by\n\n$$\nΔy={y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}\\cdot Δx,\n$$\n\nwith ${y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}=f({x}_{\\text{new}},{y}_{\\text{new}})$ evaluated at the next $x$ and $y$ values.\n\nIn general $Δy$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δy & ={y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}\\cdot Δx \\\\  & =(({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}+2{y}_{\\text{new}})\\cdot 0.5 \\\\  & =0.5({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}+{y}_{\\text{new}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute this into ${y}_{\\text{new}}=y+Δy$ and move all terms to the left-hand side to define $g({y}_{\\text{new}}):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+Δy \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+0.5({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}+{y}_{\\text{new}} \\\\ {{{y}_{\\text{new}}-y-0.5({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}-{y}_{\\text{new}}}_{⏟}}_{g({y}_{\\text{new}})} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general form of the function $g$ for step size $Δx=0.5$ is\n\n$$\ng({y}_{\\text{new}})=-\\,y-0.5({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186353673 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6329ab32-968f-5041-b2e3-12dde408968a" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Function on Which to Apply a Root-Finding Method When Applying the Implicit Euler Method"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "20f2d2e9-2c6b-544b-ab13-60ecc8dda21d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "g({y}_{\\text{new}})=0.75{y}^{2}+{y}_{\\text{new}}-y-2.25{x}_{\\text{new}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353675} {:answer/id #uuid "f3ed478c-35c9-5a77-a22c-cb37781cdf64" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "g({y}_{\\text{new}})={y}_{\\text{new}}-y-2.25{x}_{\\text{new}}-0.75({y}_{\\text{new}})^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353676} {:answer/id #uuid "49c5784c-45a1-5808-99b3-07a0be60061f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "g({y}_{\\text{new}})=0.75({y}_{\\text{new}})^{2}-{y}_{\\text{new}}+2.25{x}_{\\text{new}}-y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353677} {:answer/id #uuid "e7c59e9e-e062-5d3b-aaeb-06eab3a729e3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "g({y}_{\\text{new}})=0.75({y}_{\\text{new}})^{2}+{y}_{\\text{new}}-y-2.25{x}_{\\text{new}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353678} {:answer/id #uuid "5b17a757-9b05-51ca-a525-914441c169b5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "g({y}_{\\text{new}})=-{y}_{\\text{new}}+y+2.25{x}_{\\text{new}}-0.75{y}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353679}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e7c59e9e-e062-5d3b-aaeb-06eab3a729e3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "g({y}_{\\text{new}})=0.75({y}_{\\text{new}})^{2}+{y}_{\\text{new}}-y-2.25{x}_{\\text{new}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353678} :answer-field/id #uuid "6e0bad87-84b4-5281-80dc-e882a31ec666" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353674}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "43774789-c34c-506f-b225-3746f175168c" :question/math-academy-id "q-333106" :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=3x-{y}^{2},\\,y(0)=2\n$$\n\nUsing the implicit Euler method with step size $Δx=0.75,$ the new value ${y}_{\\text{new}}$ is obtained by solving the equation $g({y}_{\\text{new}})=0$ at each step.\nWhich of the following is the **general form** of $g({y}_{\\text{new}})$ in terms of the new values ${x}_{\\text{new}}$ and ${y}_{\\text{new}},$ and the current value $y?$" :question/worked-solution "For an initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=f(x,y),\\,{y}_{0}=y({x}_{0}),\n$$\n\nthe implicit Euler method with step size $Δx$ is given by\n\n$$\nΔy={y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}\\cdot Δx,\n$$\n\nwith ${y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}=f({x}_{\\text{new}},{y}_{\\text{new}})$ evaluated at the next $x$ and $y$ values.\n\nIn general $Δy$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δy & ={y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}\\cdot Δx \\\\  & =(3{x}_{\\text{new}}-({y}_{\\text{new}})^{2})\\cdot 0.75 \\\\  & =2.25{x}_{\\text{new}}-0.75({y}_{\\text{new}})^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute this into ${y}_{\\text{new}}=y+Δy$ and move all terms to the left-hand side to define $g({y}_{\\text{new}}):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+Δy \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+2.25{x}_{\\text{new}}-0.75({y}_{\\text{new}})^{2} \\\\ {{0.75({y}_{\\text{new}})^{2}+{y}_{\\text{new}}-y-2.25{x}_{\\text{new}}}_{⏟}}_{g({y}_{\\text{new}})} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general form of the function $g$ for step size $Δx=0.75$ is\n\n$$\ng({y}_{\\text{new}})=0.75({y}_{\\text{new}})^{2}+{y}_{\\text{new}}-y-2.25{x}_{\\text{new}}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186353680 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6329ab32-968f-5041-b2e3-12dde408968a" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Function on Which to Apply a Root-Finding Method When Applying the Implicit Euler Method"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2c3f12c2-c0b0-5daf-90f4-e479d78ca368" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "g({y}_{\\text{new}})=0.5({y}_{\\text{new}})^{3}-0.125{y}_{\\text{new}}-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353682} {:answer/id #uuid "6612eba8-2d17-58e6-8790-ad600d8fa2fe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "g({y}_{\\text{new}})=0.5({y}_{\\text{new}})^{3}-0.125{y}_{\\text{new}}+3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353683} {:answer/id #uuid "c0208d98-3904-543c-a806-fa2b9424513c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "g({y}_{\\text{new}})=0.5({y}_{\\text{new}})^{3}+{y}_{\\text{new}}-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353684} {:answer/id #uuid "6d82e815-6e4d-5d4d-a346-e460c1dca513" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "g({y}_{\\text{new}})=-0.5({y}_{\\text{new}})^{3}-0.125{y}_{\\text{new}}-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353685} {:answer/id #uuid "3cd37958-a241-5be2-93db-638dee95d3c4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "g({y}_{\\text{new}})=({y}_{\\text{new}})^{3}-0.125{y}_{\\text{new}}-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353686}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2c3f12c2-c0b0-5daf-90f4-e479d78ca368" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "g({y}_{\\text{new}})=0.5({y}_{\\text{new}})^{3}-0.125{y}_{\\text{new}}-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353682} :answer-field/id #uuid "e0186698-e195-518a-9289-0b65d688ae25" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353681}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4acdd86e-feb2-5b8f-9158-a782834e3029" :question/math-academy-id "q-333119" :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}={x}^{2}y-{y}^{3},\\,y(1)=3\n$$\n\nUsing the implicit Euler method with step size $Δx=0.5,$ the new value ${y}_{\\text{new}}$ is obtained by solving the equation $g({y}_{\\text{new}})=0$ at each step.\nWhich of the following is the **specific function** $g({y}_{\\text{new}})$ used in the first step?" :question/worked-solution "For an initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=f(x,y),\\,{y}_{0}=y({x}_{0}),\n$$\n\nthe implicit Euler method with step size $Δx$ is given by\n\n$$\nΔy={y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}\\cdot Δx,\n$$\n\nwith ${y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}=f({x}_{\\text{new}},{y}_{\\text{new}})$ evaluated at the next $x$ and $y$ values.\n\nIn general, $Δy$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δy & ={y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}\\cdot Δx \\\\  & =(({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}{y}_{\\text{new}}-({y}_{\\text{new}})^{3})\\cdot 0.5 \\\\  & =0.5({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}{y}_{\\text{new}}-0.5({y}_{\\text{new}})^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute this into ${y}_{\\text{new}}=y+Δy$ and move all terms to the left-hand side and define the resulting expression as $g({y}_{\\text{new}}):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+Δy \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+0.5({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}{y}_{\\text{new}}-0.5({y}_{\\text{new}})^{3} \\\\ {{0.5({y}_{\\text{new}})^{3}+{y}_{\\text{new}}-0.5({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}{y}_{\\text{new}}-y}_{⏟}}_{g({y}_{\\text{new}})} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the general form of the function $g$ for step size $Δx=0.5$ is\n\n$$\ng({y}_{\\text{new}})=0.5({y}_{\\text{new}})^{3}+{y}_{\\text{new}}-0.5({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}{y}_{\\text{new}}-y.\n$$\n\nNow, in the first step, the new $x$ value is ${x}_{\\text{new}}=x+Δx=1+0.5=1.5.$ Therefore, the function used in the first step is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g({y}_{\\text{new}}) & =0.5({y}_{\\text{new}})^{3}+{y}_{\\text{new}}-0.5\\cdot (1.5)^{2}{y}_{\\text{new}}-3 \\\\  & =0.5({y}_{\\text{new}})^{3}+{y}_{\\text{new}}-1.125{y}_{\\text{new}}-3 \\\\  & =0.5({y}_{\\text{new}})^{3}-0.125{y}_{\\text{new}}-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186353687 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "866481fb-c460-5a39-a7a0-84b64d8bd673" :knowledge-point/title "Approximating the Solution to an Initial Value Problem Using the Implicit Euler Method: One Step"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "02eb2b7c-6285-5949-bebc-240ddfbbcec9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.75" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353689} {:answer/id #uuid "a36092b9-0d69-51bc-80f8-e813b6b6e88b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.65" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353690}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a36092b9-0d69-51bc-80f8-e813b6b6e88b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.65" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353690} :answer-field/id #uuid "3cd54c34-cdff-5b54-b61f-3c9c69381425" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353688}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2b04598d-7f01-5a4d-adbb-3db42072dfa0" :question/math-academy-id "q-333293" :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}={x}^{2}-{y}^{2},\\,y(1.5)=1\n$$\n\nUse the implicit Euler method with one step and Newton's method to approximate $y(2).$ Round your answer to two decimal places.\n\n$y(2)≈$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "For an initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=f(x,y),\\,{y}_{0}=y({x}_{0}),\n$$\n\nthe implicit Euler method with step size $Δx$ is given by\n\n$$\nΔy={y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}\\cdot Δx,\n$$\n\nwith ${y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}=f({x}_{\\text{new}},{y}_{\\text{new}})$ evaluated at the next $x$ and $y$ values.\n\nSince we want to find the value of $y$ at $x=2,$ we will use a step size of\n\n$$\nΔx=2-1.5=0.5.\n$$\n\nNow, let's proceed with the implicit Euler method. In general, $Δy$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δy & ={y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}\\cdot Δx \\\\  & =(({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}-({y}_{\\text{new}})^{2})\\cdot 0.5 \\\\  & =0.5({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}-0.5({y}_{\\text{new}})^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute this into ${y}_{\\text{new}}=y+Δy$ and move all terms to the left-hand side and define the resulting expression as $g({y}_{\\text{new}}):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+Δy \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+0.5({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}-0.5({y}_{\\text{new}})^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives the equation\n\n$$\n0.5({y}_{\\text{new}})^{2}+{y}_{\\text{new}}-y-0.5({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}=0.\n$$\n\nSo, the general form of the function $g$ for step size $Δx=0.5$ is\n\n$$\ng({y}_{\\text{new}})=0.5({y}_{\\text{new}})^{2}+{y}_{\\text{new}}-y-0.5({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}.\n$$\n\nNow, in the first step, the new $x$ value is ${x}_{\\text{new}}=x+Δx=1.5+0.5=2.$ Then, the function $g$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g({y}_{\\text{new}}) & =0.5({y}_{\\text{new}})^{2}+{y}_{\\text{new}}-1-0.5(2)^{2} \\\\  & =0.5({y}_{\\text{new}})^{2}+{y}_{\\text{new}}-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe use a root-finding method with starting point $y=1$ to solve $g({y}_{\\text{new}})=0.$ We'll use Newton's method. \n\n$$\n({y}_{\\text{new}})_{n+1}=({y}_{\\text{new}})_{n}-\\frac{g({y}_{\\text{new}})}{{g}^{′}({y}_{\\text{new}})}\n$$\n\nNote that the derivative of $g$ is\n\n$$\n{g}^{′}({y}_{\\text{new}})=({y}_{\\text{new}})+1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, our Newton's method iterative scheme is as follows:\n\n$$\n({y}_{\\text{new}})_{n+1}=({y}_{\\text{new}})_{n}-\\frac{0.5(({y}_{\\text{new}})_{n})^{2}+({y}_{\\text{new}})_{n}-3}{(({y}_{\\text{new}})_{n})+1}\n$$\n\nApplying several iterations of Newton's method starting with $y(1.5)=1,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({y}_{\\text{new}})_{1} & =1 \\\\ ({y}_{\\text{new}})_{2} & =1.750000 \\\\ ({y}_{\\text{new}})_{3} & ≈1.647727 \\\\ ({y}_{\\text{new}})_{4} & ≈1.645752\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that $y(2)≈1.65,$ rounded to two decimal places."}]}
